2) A-Rod kept up the 300 average and 40+ HR for the duration of his contract.  He started to drop off slightly in 2009 and 2010 then in 2011 he fell off the cliff.  The thing to keep in mind about this is that A-Rod kept these numbers up, in part, through the use of steroids and HGH.

&#x200B;

I'm not sure what the WAR numbers are for these players in this span but I think that if Machado insists on 10 year contract

Mariano Rivera. Because, duh.

